            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think It Over"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.72,
            0.287,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why do suspended particles settle in muddy water over time but not in milk?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.786,
            0.296,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How is evaporation different from boiling?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.82,
            0.294,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why do you see bright rays of sunlight when it passes through small gaps between the leaves of a dense tree?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.686,
            0.89,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Have you ever wondered how sweet, white crystals of sugar are obtained from tall, green sugarcane plants? Or how do doctors detect diseases like malaria using just a few drops of blood? Many such everyday activities are made possible by techniques based on the fascinating science of separating mixtures."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.328,
            0.777,
            0.405,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
